-### TTFT difference between `new` and `head`: which change causes it
-
-`head` is the 2026-09-17 binary. `new` differs from it in two ways: the typed K owner and views (this port), and 916 `main` commits that came in with the merge. Several of those commits touch the attention and scheduler hot path (query splitting, attention path stats, the chunk-size removal, K and V projections on separate device halves). The typed port changes no stored byte and no kernel. So the hypothesis is that the TTFT difference comes from `main`.
-
-The measurement that separates the two: a third binary, `headm` = commit c6ec38813d of this branch. It has the merge of `main` and the raw-pointer K plane of the previous head, but not the typed port. It runs against `new` on the same cells (CPU attention prompt 1024 and 8192, FPGA attention prompt 1024, 8 users, 3 repetitions), after a token-identity smoke (`headm` must equal `new` for 256 tokens).
-
-Verdict rule: if `headm` sits inside `new`'s band in every cell, the TTFT difference is `main`'s and the port costs nothing. If `headm` is slower than `new` beyond the band, the port itself changed prefill time, and the cause is looked for in the port.
-
